// the student already owns (level 1, every line given), and the lesson's build
// is the HUD, which reads `StatManager.original.health` etc. There is no axe
// flag in the build, so all axe references are gone — 5.1's axe pickup stays a
// player-side bool until a lesson gives it a home.
//
// Scaffolding: FULL WALKTHROUGH (level 1) — TWO of them, both level 1, because
// neither mechanism is code the student has written before: reading the object
// that survives a load, and driving a TextMeshPro label from it. verify-site
// reads the level from EVERY walkthrough on the page and refuses a page whose
// walkthroughs disagree. The DECOMPOSE block is level 1 too.
//
// Answer-box ids are positional and persisted, so the socratic block keeps its
// three questions in order and the decompose block keeps both of its turns.
